From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flax <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 21:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fbtp: add stepwise hysteresis to stop idle fan oscillation

On an idle TiogaPass at ~25.5 C ambient the fans cycled between roughly 35% and
70% on an ~8 second period, loud enough to be obvious across the room.

It is not PID hunting.  Sampling the zone showed two exact discrete PWM values,
89/255 (35%) and 178/255 (70%), which are two adjacent entries of the
MB_INLET_TEMP_STP stepwise table:

    Reading: 20 22 24 26 28 30 32 34 36 38  40
    Output:  13 14 16 17 18 19 23 26 30 35  70

MB_INLET_REMOTE_TEMP sits at 40.0 C and dithers +/-0.125 C, so every sample that
crosses the last boundary flips the fans between 35% and 70%:

    inlet=39.875 -> pwm 89      inlet=40.125 -> pwm 178
    inlet=39.938 -> pwm 89      inlet=40.000 -> pwm 178

Every stepwise controller in this config had PositiveHysteresis and
NegativeHysteresis of 0, so there is nothing to suppress the flapping.  Give all
seven 2.0 C of hysteresis, which is well outside the observed dither.  The other
six (DTS_CPU*, DIMM_*) do not trigger at current temperatures -- their tables
start at 73 C and 65 C -- but they have the same latent defect.

Not addressed here, deliberately, as they are judgement calls rather than bugs:
  - the last step is a cliff, 35% -> 70% in one 2 C move, where every other step
    changes by 1-5 points;
  - MB_INLET_REMOTE_TEMP reads ~40 C at 25.5 C ambient, a 14 C rise on an idle
    machine, which suggests the sensor is not really at the inlet or is
    miscalibrated.  If it reads high the whole table is shifted and the box runs
    louder than designed at every ambient.

Signed-off-by: Flax <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
---
--- a/configurations/fbtp.json
+++ b/configurations/fbtp.json
@@ -559,7 +559,7 @@
         "MB_INLET_REMOTE_TEMP"
       ],
       "Name": "MB_INLET_TEMP_STP",
-      "NegativeHysteresis": 0,
+      "NegativeHysteresis": 2.0,
       "Output": [
         13.0,
         14.0,
@@ -573,7 +573,7 @@
         35.0,
         70.0
       ],
-      "PositiveHysteresis": 0,
+      "PositiveHysteresis": 2.0,
